# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Kinesis Cars — environment variables
#
# PUBLIC_API_URL   Base URL of the Kinesis Cars REST API. The `PUBLIC_` prefix
#                  tells Astro to expose it to client-side code; it is inlined
#                  into the static build at build time.
#
#   Local development  → /x/cars/
#       A same-origin relative path, forwarded by the Vite dev proxy in
#       astro.config.mjs to http://localhost:8080/x/cars/. This avoids CORS
#       in the browser during development.
#
#   Production         → https://api.kinesis.world/x/cars/
#       Served as-is (see note below about proxying in production).
#
# PUBLIC_MEDIA_ORIGIN
#       Origin for media URLs (`<origin>/<path>`), the API host WITHOUT the
#       `/x/cars/` path. Media is displayed via <img>, which is not subject to
#       CORS, so this stays an absolute cross-origin URL.
#
#   Local development  → http://localhost:8080
#   Production         → https://api.kinesis.world
#
# PUBLIC_UPLOAD_ORIGIN
#       Base for the upload POST. The endpoint is `POST /upload` (not under
#       `/x/cars/`). The API does not send `Access-Control-Allow-Origin`, so
#       uploads are proxied same-origin instead:
#         - dev:  PUBLIC_UPLOAD_ORIGIN=""  → browser posts to `/upload`, the
#                 Vite dev proxy forwards to http://localhost:8080/upload
#         - prod: PUBLIC_UPLOAD_ORIGIN=""  → browser posts to `/upload`, nginx
#                 proxies to https://api.kinesis.world/upload
#                 (see the `location /upload` block in nginx.conf.template)
#
# Copy this file to `.env` and adjust as needed. `.env` is gitignored.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

PUBLIC_API_URL=/x/cars/
PUBLIC_MEDIA_ORIGIN=http://localhost:8080
PUBLIC_UPLOAD_ORIGIN=